<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1976–2009</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as LTTE, Tamil Tigers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam were a Tamil separatist militant organisation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, founded in 1976 by Velupillai Prabhakaran to create an independent Tamil state, Tamil Eelam, in the north and east. During the civil war from 1983 they controlled large areas, ran a de facto administration and used suicide bombings and child soldiers. The Sri Lankan army defeated them in May 2009, when Prabhakaran was killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberation-tigers-of-tamil-eelam.jpg" alt="Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tyiqnqnenq · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tamil_Eelam_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
